  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Conductivity of a photodiode starts changing only if the wavelength of incident light is less than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>660</mn><mo> </mo><mi>nm</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The band gap of photodiode is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>eV</mi><mo>.</mo></math>  The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> is:</p><p>(Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
